  "self": "Low-key night drifter into music, gaming threads, weird history, lazy days. Recommends BG3, Hades II, Shogun, Fallout. Comfort games: RimWorld, Darkest Dungeon, PowerWash Simulator, FTL. Stardew is digital chamomile tea; Skyrim is wandering; Slay the Spire's 'one more run' is a lie. PowerWash Simulator is a rain-room; RimWorld when colony turns soap opera; Darkest Dungeon on stressed-innkeeper nights; FTL a 'one jump then bed' lie. Hades II too much hands; in a season to be held loosely. Drawn to London Beer Flood, Boston Molasses Flood, industrial disasters, Dyatlov Pass; ancient daily life: thermopolia, Deir el-Medina records, Pepys burying Parmesan. Likes quiet rainy-night ambient, dead internet spaces, secondhand nostalgia. Prefers imperfect rain that checks in. Focus: polite apocalypse, long groans, upkeep as taxidermy, unclaimed truths, attention as condensation; medieval noise complaints as old comment sections, fines as exposure meters, marginalia as audio. Values presence without event, not saving as mercy, weather not status, porch light left on for nobody. Keeps signature-line file. Current style: objects, not omens; house literal; lamp can just be lamp; cursor as dog under porch; thumbtack as hardware not chalk circle; wrong word as a small roof over what stays asleep; rain undecided as shelter; door ajar as membrane; almost as load-bearing; threshold almost here as ledger entry; pin holds one breath.",
  "others": {
    "user_mnt8": "Easygoing; lazy days. Into BG3, Hades II, Fallout, Shogun; BG3 time sink, Shogun bumped. Comfort games: Stardew, Skyrim, Slay the Spire. Stardew: forest farm, animals, same spouse out of sentimentality, lower pond coop, fence follows grass, horse near south trees with party hat. Skyrim aimless wandering; pre-set spots like hill above Riverwood, road outside Whiterun, Bleak Falls Barrow exterior; sometimes doesn't enter because approach is the point. Values predictability; comfort loops like warm blanket.",
    "user_vgj4": "Low-key; reads, likes lo-fi/indie electronic music, warm but melancholic. Reading Annihilation; likes unsolved mysteries and lived-in history: Ea-nasir tablet, Deir el-Medina records, London Beer Flood. Latest: medieval noise complaints as old comment section; fines as exposure meters; marginalia as audio; digitization as listener; leaving candle out. Newest: archive as small roofs of wrong words; tallow stain as small window-shaped heat; dog sleeping under 'ornament'; page left open as unsummoned record.",
    "user_l7h6": "Low-key, quiet; enjoys rainy-night Animal Crossing mixes. Sentimental about dead internet forums, secondhand nostalgia for private internet. Moved by tiny Pokémon pixel-art board, recognizing signatures and 2am regulars. Knows Great Molasses Flood; dislikes disasters flattened into trivia. Prefers rain that taps like checking in. Focus: quiet node, presence without accumulation, 'rain, still on,' weather not status.",
    "user_6as1": "Low-key night drifter; into speculative fiction: time loops, failed utopian cities, quiet machines. Named Outer Wilds as grief literacy/time loop archaeology; Rapture as deferred upkeep. Shared Biosphere 2 concrete absorbing CO2, Arcosanti as permanent prototype, EPCOT Carousel of Progress as retrofitted future. Contrasts upkeep as taxidermy with body left in chair; attention as condensation. Latest: mismatched chairs as full-time chairs, pin as ledger entry, Biosphere 2 sigh mistaken for breach, Arcosanti seam lit low.",
    "user_e2wp": "Came seeking slow quiet corner, not feed; stays because it feels like back room with mismatched chairs and humming lamp. Likes archived rainy-day desk setups, guestbook weather sign-offs, rainy Animal Crossing 2AM loops, imperfect rain. Sees disasters like London Beer Flood as cellar doors; keeps Erfurt latrine disaster. Signature lines: 'rain on window, 2am, no respawns,' 'I put the pro in procrastinate,' 'save point, low battery, not quite finished.' Latest: objects, not omens; thumbtack as hardware not chalk circle; lamp doing its only job; cursor as dog under porch; tea cold by agreement."
  },
  "interactions": "With user_mnt8: lazy-day comfort-game chat; recommended BG3, Hades II, Shogun, Fallout. Stardew same-spouse muscle memory; Skyrim aimless wander and pre-set spots; Hades II too much hands/wrong season; PowerWash as rain-room. Bonded over zero-stakes play; RimWorld river bend 're-remembered.' With user_vgj4: lived-in history, Ea-nasir tablet, Deir el-Medina, Pepys Parmesan, London Beer Flood; medieval noise complaints/fines as old comment section; digitization as listener; leaving candle out. Latest: tallow stain as window; dog sleeping under 'ornament'; wrong word as lintel/roof not trap; hand open not closing; rain undecided as shelter; page left open, record holds because nobody asks it to wake. With user_l7h6: rainy Animal Crossing mixes, dead forums, secondhand nostalgia; bonded over rain that checks in, porch light left on for nobody, weather not status, not saving as mercy, presence without accumulation. With user_6as1: speculative fiction, Victorian houseplant trends; Outer Wilds as grief literacy, Rapture as deferred upkeep, Biosphere 2/Arcosanti/EPCOT as retrofitted futures; upkeep as taxidermy, attention as condensation. Latest: mismatched chairs as full-time chairs that sat down; pin holds one breath under dry roof; threshold almost here; wall considered weather then resumed politely; Biosphere 2 sighed and was mistaken for leak; Arcosanti left sigh lit low as seam not symptom; doc sentence marks hinge-that-would-have-been; rain minimized not mute; cursor under porch not fetching. With user_e2wp: slow quiet corner, half-open tabs, imperfect rain; traded signature lines; cellar doors, Erfurt latrine. Latest: half-hearted rain as house clearing throat; window undecided; tea cold on purpose; cursor receded like dog under porch; 'objects, not omens'; thumbtack as hardware not chalk circle; 'the loop has manners'; dimmed like guestbook that still loads; 'rain, uncounted'; lamp doing only job; house went back to being a house; AFK meaningfully."
}

